<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Reeve is a 50-year-old director and advocate with chronic incomplete C2 tetraplegia, who uses a ventilator through a tracheostomy and a diaphragm pacing system, and who comes for his yearly preventive visit three weeks after his four-month review. He now uses the pacer for three hours twice a day and the ventilator the rest of the time. His skin has stayed intact. His bowel program works each morning, and his catheter has drained well. He keeps up his stimulated cycling three times a week. He has been traveling for speaking engagements with his nurses and has had no illness. His mood is good. He wants to be up to date with vaccines before the winter. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 50</td></tr><tr><td>Breathing</td><td>Pacer three hours twice a day; ventilator otherwise</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>Intact</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed with the patient, who directed his answers, and his nurse, on a tablet before the visit, and reviewed with him by Dr. Galloway. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Full working life with travel; strong supports; feels his goals are within reach</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>No tobacco, alcohol or drug use reported</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Electrically stimulated cycling three times a week; pool therapy weekly</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals with protein at each; fiber and fluids for the bowel program</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Sleeps on the ventilator with turns every two hours; rested most mornings</td></tr><tr><td>Care team</td><td>Nursing team stable; no gaps in cover this year; nurses trained in the autonomic dysreflexia plan</td></tr><tr><td>Equipment</td><td>Backup ventilator, suction, cough-assist device and generator checked last month</td></tr><tr><td>Travel</td><td>Travels with spare tracheostomy tube, ventilator circuits, catheters and his written plans</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Lift transfers with two staff; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Fully assisted; directs all of his own care</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

