<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. PCV20, the first recombinant zoster dose, RSV vaccine and Tdap given today; HIV and hepatitis C screening sent; stool immunochemical test kit given. [S]<list><item>Second zoster dose in two to six months.</item><item>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines and the first hepatitis B dose at the six-month review.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic incomplete C2 tetraplegia (G82.52)</content>. Stable; no autonomic dysreflexia; skin intact. He chose to complete advance care planning today. [S]<list><item>Continue the current plans.</item><item>Six-month review in six weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Ventilator dependence with diaphragm pacing (Z99.11)</content>. Pacer three hours twice a day; vaccines today lower his risk from respiratory infections. [S]<list><item>Continue the conditioning schedule with Dr. Kovac.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>102/62 mmHg, his usual baseline after cervical injury; a rise of 20 to 40 mmHg above it may mean autonomic dysreflexia</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Asked; no alcohol use reported</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Stool immunochemical test chosen with him, because bowel preparation for colonoscopy would need a hospital stay with his ventilator and bowel program; kit given today</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Once for adults 15 to 65; sent today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Once for adults 18 to 79; sent today</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>A1c 5.5% at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and statin assessment</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL 104, HDL 34 mg/dL at intake; estimated 10-year risk low; spinal cord injury raises cardiometabolic risk, so lipids are repeated yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Shared decision-making begins at 55</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20, recommended for all adults 50 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 of 2 today; dose 2 in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single dose; increased risk because of ventilator dependence</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap; no booster recorded within ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>At the six-month review in October</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>No record of vaccination; series to start at the six-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Dental and eye examinations</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Dental review in the spring; eye examination last year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2; Respiratory syncytial virus vaccine (RSVPreF3, adjuvanted); Tetanus, diphtheria, and acellular pertussis vaccine (Tdap) [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evaluation and Management of Autonomic Dysreflexia and Other Autonomic Dysfunctions: Preventing the Highs and Lows (Consortium for Spinal Cord Medicine) (2021); Identification and Management of Cardiometabolic Risk after Spinal Cord Injury: Clinical Practice Guideline for Health Care Providers (Consortium for Spinal Cord Medicine) (2018); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month review in six weeks with kidney function, a skin check, the influenza and COVID-19 vaccines and the first hepatitis B dose. HIV, hepatitis C and stool test results by phone. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-26: six-month review: respiratory care, skin, bladder and kidney surveillance, vaccines, and plans for the winter. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 30 minutes, with his consent; he directed the conversation himself. He wants full treatment, including hospital care and ventilation, for any illness that could be reversed, and wants to be told plainly what is happening and to make his own decisions whenever he can. He named a health care agent, recorded in the confidential part of the chart and not named here, and chose not to record other treatment preferences today. An emergency information sheet with his ventilator settings, the autonomic dysreflexia plan and this summary was given to him for his chair bag. To be revisited yearly or after any serious illness. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
